      <h1 id="using-sctp" class="group scroll-mt-20">Using the Stream Control Transmission Protocol (SCTP)<a href="#using-sctp" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>As a cluster administrator, you can use the Stream Control Transmission Protocol (SCTP) on a bare-metal cluster.</p>
      <h2 id="nw-sctp-about_using-sctp" class="group scroll-mt-20">Support for SCTP on OpenShift Container Platform<a href="#nw-sctp-about_using-sctp" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p>As a cluster administrator, you can enable SCTP on the hosts in the cluster. On Red Hat Enterprise Linux CoreOS (RHCOS), the SCTP module is disabled by default.</p>
      <p>SCTP is a reliable message based protocol that runs on top of an IP network.</p>
      <p>When enabled, you can use SCTP as a protocol with pods, services, and network policy. A <code>Service</code> object must be defined with the <code>type</code> parameter set to either the <code>ClusterIP</code> or <code>NodePort</code> value.</p>
      <h3 id="example_configurations_using-sctp" class="group scroll-mt-20">Example configurations using SCTP protocol<a href="#example_configurations_using-sctp" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <p>You can configure a pod or service to use SCTP by setting the <code>protocol</code> parameter to the <code>SCTP</code> value in the pod or service object.</p>
      <p>In the following example, a pod is configured to use SCTP:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  namespace: project1\n  name: example-pod\nspec:\n  containers:\n    - name: example-pod\n...\n      ports:\n        - containerPort: 30100\n          name: sctpserver\n          protocol: SCTP"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>In the following example, a service is configured to use SCTP:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata:\n  namespace: project1\n  name: sctpserver\nspec:\n...\n  ports:\n    - name: sctpserver\n      protocol: SCTP\n      port: 30100\n      targetPort: 30100\n  type: ClusterIP"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>In the following example, a <code>NetworkPolicy</code> object is configured to apply to SCTP network traffic on port <code>80</code> from any pods with a specific label:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"kind: NetworkPolicy\napiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nmetadata:\n  name: allow-sctp-on-http\nspec:\n  podSelector:\n    matchLabels:\n      role: web\n  ingress:\n  - ports:\n    - protocol: SCTP\n      port: 80"} lang="yaml" />
      <h2 id="nw-sctp-enabling_using-sctp" class="group scroll-mt-20">Enabling Stream Control Transmission Protocol (SCTP)<a href="#nw-sctp-enabling_using-sctp" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p>As a cluster administrator, you can load and enable the blacklisted SCTP kernel module on worker nodes in your cluster.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>Install the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>Access to the cluster as a user with the <code>cluster-admin</code> role.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create a file named <code>load-sctp-module.yaml</code> that contains the following YAML definition:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: machineconfiguration.openshift.io/v1\nkind: MachineConfig\nmetadata:\n  name: load-sctp-module\n  labels:\n    machineconfiguration.openshift.io/role: worker\nspec:\n  config:\n    ignition:\n      version: 3.2.0\n    storage:\n      files:\n        - path: /etc/modprobe.d/sctp-blacklist.conf\n          mode: 0644\n          overwrite: true\n          contents:\n            source: data:,\n        - path: /etc/modules-load.d/sctp-load.conf\n          mode: 0644\n          overwrite: true\n          contents:\n            source: data:,sctp"} lang="yaml" />
      </li>
      <li>
      To create the <code>MachineConfig</code> object, enter the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f load-sctp-module.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Optional: To watch the status of the nodes while the MachineConfig Operator applies the configuration change, enter the following command. When the status of a node transitions to <code>Ready</code>, the configuration update is applied.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get nodes"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
